{
  "scenario": "The arrival of a fictional container vessel, the Saltmarsh Trader, at the berth of a fictional port, Eastmere, on 2 October 2026. The data has the vessel's owner, a commercial organization, Larkspur Shipping, with its legal name, commercial role and capability, and the act of ownership that realizes it; the Eastmere port authority, a government organization within the council's government, delimited by its district; the vessel's master, who is employed by Larkspur, and a deckhand, who make up the crew, and a port officer, each an agent and organization member with a capability and roles; the vessel, with its proper name painted on the hull, its IMO number, and its length, measured in metres, CCO's Meter Measurement Unit; the port, on the shore, and the berth, whose spatial region is designated by coordinates recorded in WGS 84 latitude and longitude; the cargo voyage, whose arrival at the berth the master carries out in an operator role, in an interval within the day, week, month, year and decade, with the date recorded in the logbook; and the arrival report the master sends the port authority.",
